---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactLinks from '../components/ContactLinks.astro';
---

<Base title="Matthew Rossi">

  <div class="home-header">
    <div class="home-header-name">
      <img src="/profile.jpg" alt="Matthew Rossi" class="avatar" width="72" height="72">
      <h1>Matthew Rossi</h1>
      <span class="location">Brooklyn, New York</span>
    </div>
    <ol class="tagline-variants">
      <li>Urbanist and software engineer.</li>
      <li>Urbanist with thirteen years in software engineering.</li>
      <li>Urbanist. Heading to Lisbon for a master's in sustainable urban mobility.</li>
      <li>Urbanist. Software engineer for thirteen years.</li>
      <li>Urbanist. Software engineer for thirteen years, now turning toward sustainable urban mobility.</li>
    </ol>
    <ContactLinks />
  </div>

  <style>
    .tagline-variants {
      max-width: 560px;
      margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .tagline-variants li {
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
    .tagline-variants li::marker {
      color: var(--muted);
    }
  </style>

  <section id="about" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
    <h2 id="about-heading">About</h2>
    <p>I grew up outside Detroit — a place built almost entirely around the car. The near-total absence of alternatives made the connection between transportation and daily life hard to ignore. That stuck with me, and eventually became a serious interest in how cities move people and what happens when they can't.</p>
    <p>I spent thirteen years in software engineering, working across payments, financial services, and cloud infrastructure. Now I'm shifting focus to urban mobility through graduate study at the EIT Urban Mobility Master School, starting autumn 2026.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="now" aria-labelledby="now-heading">
    <h2 id="now-heading">Now</h2>
    <p>Senior Software Engineer at <a href="https://www.heroku.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Heroku (Salesforce)</a> in New York through May 2026.</p>
    <p>Starting autumn 2026, I'll be in the <strong>EIT Urban Mobility Master's Program (SUMT)</strong> — a two-year double degree, first at Técnico Lisboa in Lisbon, then at UPC BarcelonaTech in Barcelona.</p>
  </section>

</Base>
